    <statement><p>Consider the solid that lies above the square (in the <m>xy</m>-plane)
<m>R = [0, 1] \times [0, 1]</m>,
 and below the elliptic paraboloid 
<m>z = 64 - x^2+ 4 xy - 2 y^2</m>.</p>
<p>Estimate the volume by dividing <m>R</m> into 9 equal squares and choosing the
sample points to lie in the midpoints of each square.</p>
<p><fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
